      "side": 1,
      "message": "Continuing the discussion from aosp/4043296:\n\n\u003e The `share_ro` flag needs to be passed to admit_host_page. So just confirming if you were referring to changing `admit_host_page` signature and pass share_ro as an extra arg to `topup_pkvm_memcache` and update `kvm_topup_pkvm_memcache` as well ? I feel its cleaner to have it a struct passed in to `admit_host_page` and then my initial idea would not add any more complexity than having share_ro and mc wrapped in a struct. WDYT?\n\nI agree that a struct is better, and that wasn\u0027t my point. My idea is just to add a `bool share_ro` field to this struct here, instead of this `donate` callback field.\n\nMy point is that it merely happens that we have those 2 similar functions `pkvm_host_donate_hyp()` and `pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro()`, it\u0027s unlikely that we\u0027ll have any other donate functions with exactly the same signature, so this `pkvm_memcache_donate_fn_t` seems like a bit overgeneralized ad-hoc solution rather than a useful abstraction. So it seems the code would be simpler if we do it the straightforward way: add a `share_ro` flag to this struct and use `ret \u003d share_ro ? pkvm_host_donate_hyp_share_ro(...) ? pkvm_host_donate_hyp(...)` in `admit_host_page()`.",
      "revId": "562d5aa9229a87e99443a1123e807cd3c4bfd0b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
